[Applause]  oh my gosh  first i have to ask why quit your job  on social media with an audience i love  that you did it  what was that all about well i always  like to let people know that it wasn't  like i just quit with no plan  suddenly i'd been planning for a really  long time  and documenting and sharing my  entrepreneurial journey  so it just felt authentic to also share  this part  it's the scariest part for a lot of  people and i wanted to be true to form  so i did it and was there a plan  or a hope that it would inspire others  or is this just what you needed to do  for yourself  maybe a little a column a and a little a  column b right you know  some of it was definitely that i'm the  type of girl where  i needed to scorch that bridge down so  that i wouldn't end up  running back across it when i was scared  but then the other side is i wanted to  really paint a picture of what it looks  like to step into entrepreneurship  that i really wanted people to see the  journey from the beginning and see that  yeah  it's scary but you can still show up  every single day you  say that you can have it all but not at  the same  time yes so it's  more that you can't be all the things to  all the people  all the time right so my big thing is  i spend a lot of my focus on identifying  which  ball i can drop because some balls are  made of glass  and some balls are made of rubber the  glass ones are going to shatter and the  rubber ones are going to bounce back but  no matter what you're going to juggle  them and you're going to drop the ball  so for me it's about knowing which one's  which if i have to miss a carpool pickup  well that's rubber it'll bounce back  i can make it up a different day but if  i have to miss a  milestone recital or a really big  doctor's appointment  well that's glass and i want to make  sure i prioritize those so i can show up  but then let's also grant ourselves some  grace  we're not always going to get it right  you know what's so ironic nicole i love  that you said that  i can give everybody else grace by the  way i have it written on my hands  literally i wrote it down on my hand and  i've been writing it because it's  something that i really lack for myself  i think that's so powerful and  especially as you know  we're both moms of daughters you know i  always think about  my kids are watching me and if they  don't see me extending myself grace and  saying you know what i'm really tired i  think i'm gonna turn in early or  honestly i did my best with this project  i'm just gonna go ahead and let it sit  and try again tomorrow  how on earth will our daughters learn  how to do it for themselves so  i love the idea of putting grace right  in front of you  where you're not going to forget to  extend it all day long  well i actually happen to know how much  your daughters look up to you  check out this mother's day surprise  happy mother's day we just want to let  you know how much you mean to us  and thank you for helping us grow and  become the people that we are today  thank you for helping me talk about my  feelings better  and i want to thank you because you were  the woman who showed me that  i can be gracious and kind while also  following my dreams and being true to  myself  you are a very silly and weird person  we love you bye oh my gosh  you're gonna make me lose my lashes  i love it i hope they run in that river  right away from you  just being a mom is such it's so  important to me because  as an adoptive mother um you know our  family is really special and  we're meant to be together and hearing  that just really  it's just nice to know that they know  how much i love them  were you jeez drew will you speak to me  a little bit about that nicole  about your um family dynamic  we actually met our daughters when their  mother was panhandling  on the side of the street in baltimore  um we pulled over to just kind of  see what was going on and we found out  that  it was a tough situation so we offered  to  me and my husband just will mentor we'll  bring groceries we'll kind of stand  in the gap where we can and uh within 30  days we found out that their mother was  going to be incarcerated  so uh we wanted to make sure the girls  stayed together and so we took them in  and a year later uh we all kind of  decided  with their mother their bio mom included  that it was best if they stuck around  with us  and here we are six years later and i'm  a mom to  three girls ages 9 18 and 22.  nicole when i  was lucky enough to get this job and  it's something i don't take for granted  any day because i just didn't want to be  the kind of mom that wasn't with my kids  you know i needed to have a job that  made me feel like  my kids come first and i just really  have the greatest admiration for you  i love your story i love what a good  person you are  being this brave woman like a fearless  leader who takes on so much and yet  you're a great role model as a mother  and to  all of us other mothers and just women  in general  oh drew you're amazing thank you so much  um it's  a joy to be able to share you know she's  the boss on usa network so that people  can see  that families are made in a lot of  different ways and we're imperfect and  we're doing the best we can  and it's all good enough  yeah it really is nicole and so are you  thank you nicole walters she's the boss  episodes are available on usanetwork.com  and the usa network app

